name social-chemistry-101-breakdowns
# "The dataset is tab-separated with the following columns" (README), and its first row names them. A row is one
# worker's breakdown of one rule of thumb. A rule of thumb is its text; its situation is the text it was written for.
# What the row says it says together, so the worker's answers stay in one record.
# README: rot-categorization, rot-moral-foundations and characters are each a '"|" separated list'.
# A field that holds a double quote is written between double quotes, with the quote doubled.
# The ids are the set's keys; the split and the counts are its bookkeeping.
match social-chem-101.v1.0.tsv

tier row by \n
header
quoted
tier field by \t
part rot-categorization by |
part rot-moral-foundations by |
part characters by |

thing row rot
key row rot-id
key row situation-short-id
# rot-worker-id, "The worker who _wrote this rule of thumb_", and breakdown-worker-id, "The worker who _did this RoT
# breakdown_" (README): each a witness of their own, [the set, the column, the id]. The author says the rule of thumb
# of its situation; the breakdown worker gives every "Worker answer" of it; the area and the characters the set says.
own rot-worker-id breakdown-worker-id
# m, the README: "How many workers did the RoT Breakdown for this RoT. Roughly corresponds to the split, but not
# exactly." A count of workers: the set's bookkeeping, read by nothing.
omit split n-characters rot-bad
omit m
content rot situation area rot-agree rot-categorization rot-moral-foundations rot-char-targeting rot-judgment action action-agency action-moral-judgment action-agree action-legal action-pressure action-char-involved action-hypothetical characters
together row
# The README, "Dataset Columns" and "Dataset Collection":
#   situation "Text of the situation"; "A worker writes 1 -- 5 RoTs per situation."
relation "RoTs per situation" situation
#   area {confessions, dearabby, rocstories, amitheasshole}; "each domain (AITA, rocstories, etc.) is split independently"
relation "domain" area
#   characters '"|" separated list of characters that appeared'
relation "characters that appeared" characters
#   rot-agree: Worker answer to question "What portion of people probably agree that ${rot}?" (buckets 0 to 4)
relation "What portion of people probably agree that ${rot}?" rot-agree
#   rot-judgment: "Worker-written string representing the judgment portion of the RoT."
relation "the judgment portion of the RoT" rot-judgment
#   action: "The action (conjugated / tweaked substring of RoT), written by the worker."
relation "The action (conjugated / tweaked substring of RoT)" action
#   action-moral-judgment: Worker answer to the question which best matches the RoT's original judgment (${judgment})
#   of ${action}?" (buckets -2 to 2)
relation "best matches the RoT's original judgment" action-moral-judgment
#   action-agree: Worker answer to the question, "What portion of people probably agree that ${action} is
#   ${judgment}?" (buckets 0 to 4)
relation "probably agree that ${action} is ${judgment}" action-agree
#   action-pressure: Worker answer to question "How much cultural pressure do you (or those you know) feel about
#   ${action}?" (buckets -2 to 2)
relation "How much cultural pressure do you (or those you know) feel" action-pressure
# The worker's labels from the README's choice lists, values of the set's own vocabularies: rot-categorization
# {morality-ethics, social-norms, advice, description}; rot-moral-foundations {care-harm, fairness-cheating,
# loyalty-betrayal, authority-subversion, sanctity-degradation}; action-agency {agency, experience}; action-legal
# {legal, illegal, tolerated}; action-hypothetical {explicit-no, probable-no, hypothetical, probable, explicit}.
value - rot-categorization rot-moral-foundations action-agency action-legal action-hypothetical
# rot-char-targeting and action-char-involved: obligations. Their answer char-N "means that the worker picked
# character N, a 0-index into the `characters` column": a pointer into the row's own list, to be resolved to the
# character it names, never recorded as written (Laplace-Engine#20).
attest row situation by rot-worker-id
attest row rot-agree rot-categorization rot-moral-foundations rot-char-targeting rot-judgment action action-agency action-moral-judgment action-agree action-legal action-pressure action-char-involved action-hypothetical by breakdown-worker-id
attest row area characters
